X:7
T:Oh! Susanna
C:Stephen Foster (1848)
O:USA
M:2/4
L:1/8
K:G
N:The first verse and the chorus only, in standard spelling. Foster wrote the song for blackface minstrel shows; his original second verse uses a racial slur in a violent joke, and it is never sung here. Teach that history with the song.
G/2A/2 | B2 dd | d>e dB | G>A BB | A3 G/2A/2 | B2 dd | d>e dB | G>A BB | A2 G G/2A/2 |
w: I come from A-la-ba-ma with a ban-jo on my knee, I'm go-ing to Lou-i-si-a-na, my true love for to see. It rained
B2 dd | d>e dB | G>A BB | A3 G/2A/2 | B2 dd | d>e dB | G>A BB | A2 G2 |
w: all night the day I left, the wea-ther it was dry; the sun so hot I froze to death, Su-san-na, don't you cry. _
c2 c2 | e e2 e | d d B G | A3 G/2A/2 | B2 dd | d>e dB | G>A BB | A2 G2 |]
w: Oh! Su-san-na, oh, don't you cry for me, for I come from A-la-ba-ma with a ban-jo on my knee.

